WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.372
The curated table should not just be a copy of the raw data.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:10.197
It should have useful types, deliberate columns, and a documented row grain.

00:00:10.197 --> 00:00:14.312
For example, a monthly sales table may have one row per product and month.

00:00:14.312 --> 00:00:18.352
A readmission table may have one row per repeat admission.

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:24.777
Connect this idea to a healthcare analytics platform processing large longitudinal event tables.

00:00:24.777 --> 00:00:30.642
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:30.642 --> 00:00:38.362
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:38.362 --> 00:00:44.387
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:44.387 --> 00:00:50.240
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
